This Python program takes an integer `T` as input, which denotes the number of test cases. Each test case is a string `S`. The program then iterates through each test case, counting the number of distinct Yalalovichik substrings for each one. A substring `S[:i+1]` is considered a Yalalovichik string if it meets the criteria of having the same number of distict non-empty substrings as it does distinct non-empty subsequences. It then prints the count for each test case.

